warranty.

Base: RustDesk tag 1.5.0, commit fada664df7a294d1d1a9ca3e7cd3637069122f17,
with libs/hbb_common at commit 229b904508364c8997aad0fb5af57effac859f60
(https://github.com/rustdesk/hbb_common) included as plain files.

Modified by LoomNaru Labs Inc, starting 2026-10-16. The changes, each in its
own commit after the import commit:

1. libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs: the built-in ID server is rd.emillis.net
   instead of rs-ny.rustdesk.com, and the built-in server public key is the
   public key of rd.emillis.net instead of RustDesk's.
2. src/common.rs: when no account (API) server is saved, the app uses
   https://rd.emillis.net instead of https://admin.rustdesk.com.
3. flutter/macos and flutter/ios: bundle identifier
   com.loomnarulabs.emilliremote and display name "Emilli Remote".
4. .github/workflows: upstream's workflows are removed; build-apple.yml
   builds the Mac and iPhone apps with the same steps and versions as
   upstream's macOS and iOS jobs.
5. NOTICE, .github/README.md and docs/APPLE_SIGNING_NEXT.md are new.

Changed on 2026-10-16 for the Mac app, so that it installs next to an
official RustDesk and can never turn into one (the iPhone app is
unchanged by these, apart from shared text in item 11):

6. src/platform/privileges_scripts (install.scpt, update.scpt,
   uninstall.scpt, daemon.plist): every path is quoted, so an app name
   with a space works.
7. libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs, flutter/macos/Runner/Configs/
   AppInfo.xcconfig, build.py, build-apple.yml: on macOS the app name is
   "Emilli Remote" and the bundle is "Emilli Remote.app", with its own
   settings folder, logs, IPC sockets and launchd jobs.
8. libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs: on macOS a new device ID is the number
   desktop RustDesk derives from the network card plus 0x20000000, so it
   never equals the ID of an official RustDesk on the same Mac.
9. libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs: on macOS direct IP access
   ("direct-server") is always off and cannot be turned on.
10. libs/hbb_common/src/config.rs and lib.rs: on macOS auto update
    ("allow-auto-update") is always off, and the app has no address to
    ask RustDesk's servers for a new version.
11. flutter/lib (consts.dart, desktop_home_page.dart,
    desktop_setting_page.dart, mobile connection_page.dart): update and
    download actions open the Emilli Remote download page
    (https://rd.emillis.net/tk4zcwgwfnpgi31hoe0xb4d5/) instead of
    downloading official RustDesk; About has an "Update" link to that
    page, and its "Website" link goes to this repository.
12. build-apple.yml: the Mac build fails if RustDesk's public server, its
    version check, its download page or its GitHub releases are built in.

Everything else is unchanged upstream code. The complete history of the
changes is the git history of this repository.

"RustDesk" is the name of the upstream project. This build is not made,
endorsed or supported by the RustDesk developers. For the official RustDesk
apps, use https://rustdesk.com or https://github.com/rustdesk/rustdesk.
